def all_unique(items):
    seen = set()
    for item in items:
        if item in seen:
            return False
        seen.add(item)
    return True
```

This function checks if all elements in the input list are unique. It uses a set to keep track of the elements it has seen so far. If it encounters an element that is already in the set, it immediately returns False. If it iterates over the entire list without finding any duplicates, it returns True.
